/cost now includes sub-agent spend. Before this, anyone who delegated work with sub_agent or explore_agent saw a /cost total lower than what they actually paid, and nothing said so. Committed as aafc072e (Part of #1073). Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass.

What changed:
• Where the numbers are kept: src/prompt/sub_agent_spend.rs now keeps a running total for the whole session, alongside the existing per-run one. Both are filled at the same point, but nothing ever empties the session total. That matters because the usage record empties the per-run total once per run; if /cost emptied it too, each would take spend from the other. The per-run path behaves exactly as before. I put the total in that file, where every reader of delegated spend can see it, and the commit body says so.
• What `/cost` prints when sub-agents ran: the first line becomes Session cost (own, excluding sub-agents): $X. Then a line sub-agents: N runs, $Y (priced at each child model's rates) with their tokens, then Total including sub-agents: $X+Y.
• When a sub-agent run can't be priced: it prints cost unknown with the tokens, and the total says unknown. It never shows $0. The same applies if the session's own model has no price.
• With no delegation (the common case), /cost prints exactly what it printed before. A test compares the full string to pin that.

Tests: they live in a new sibling file, src/prompt/sub_agent_spend_session_tests.rs, and run against local stores, not the process-wide ones. They check that:
• two records both show up in the session total, and emptying the per-run total doesn't touch it;
• an unpriced run stays unpriced;
• the exact /cost lines are right in the priced, unpriced and no-delegation cases.

As a check that the tests can fail, I removed the write to the session total: the two tests that depend on it failed by name, and passed again once it was restored.

Docs: docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md has a new "Sub-agent spend" section with example output, and it lists which places still count only the session's own spend.

Still own-spend only: these are named in the commit and in a comment on #1073 with the sha, so the issue stays open:
• --output-format json
• the --cost-warn tally (record_run_cost)
• /tokens and the per-turn breakdown inside /cost
• the phase-spend totals in scripts/extract_trajectory.py
